"""DEPRECATED — superseded by 003_users_and_habits.py, do not use.

This file used to define an Alembic revision "002" that collided with
002_payments.py (also "002", also down_revision "001") — two independent
sprint branches that both assumed they were the only migration since the
initial schema. `alembic heads` reported two heads and warned "Revision 002
is present more than once", making `alembic upgrade head` ambiguous.

The real migration was renumbered to 003_users_and_habits.py (chained after
002_payments.py, since payments shipped first chronologically) on
2026-08-13. This file is intentionally left behind as a stub — deleting it
outright wasn't possible from the environment that made this fix, and an
empty stub is safer than a half-deleted migration file. It deliberately
defines no `revision`/`down_revision`, so Alembic's directory scan skips it
as not a valid migration.

Safe to actually delete whenever convenient; nothing depends on this
filename existing.
"""
